From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:45:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: sign out, and tell the account's status and
 gamertag.

LAUNCHER_SIGN_OUT forgets the user and, with device set, the device's registration too, as
removing an account does. What is already gone counts as removed: the keychain backend no longer
fails on a missing item. LAUNCHER_ACCOUNT_STATUS reads from the keychain alone whether the device
is registered and a user is signed in. It also tells whether Microsoft refused the user's token
for the last request that needed it, in which case the user must sign in again. LAUNCHER_PROFILE
gets an Xbox token for http://xboxlive.com and answers with its gamertag and no other identifier.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: account
